From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:19:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] udht: library mode with setup, stop and status

Split the daemon's main() into udht_setup(), udht_stop() and udht_status(),
so an embedder that already runs a uloop (unetd itself, when unetd and the
DHT node live in one process, as an Android app needs) can run the node on
that loop. main() is the same code behind getopt, compiled out with
-DUDHT_LIBRARY. This replaces the udht_main() entry point from
"udht: allow building as a library", whose argv interface an embedder had
to fake.

What the library mode changes beyond the split: losing unetd arms a
reconnect timer instead of ending the loop, which is not the embedder's to
end; udht_stop() frees everything a second setup would otherwise inherit
(networks given with -N, the bootstrap list, the node file name, the status
counters); the socket close is idempotent; a missing node file is no longer
fopen(NULL). udht_status() reports connection and bootstrap progress for an
embedder's UI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PVGaNeNhqp11rTLwZ9rM4J
---
 udht.c | 237 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 udht.h |  31 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 64 deletions(-)

